('source.persia.dsab.vallat1974','La triple inscription cunéiforme de la statue de Darius Ier (DSab)','SCHOLARLY_EDITION',2,'Revue d’assyriologie et d’archéologie orientale / JSTOR','François Vallat','lang.en','1974','2026-08-26','https://www.jstor.org/stable/23282203','RA 68.2, pp. 157-166; JSTOR 23282203','Article copyright applies; bibliography, locators and independent summaries only','Published edition of the DSab trilingual cuneiform inscription','Do not reproduce the modern edition or translation in bulk',0,'French scholarly edition; ancient texts in Old Persian, Elamite and Akkadian','URL_SYNTAX_VALID','Canonical bibliographic anchor for DSab; exact line-level collation remains open where the accessible record does not expose the full edition.'),
('source.egypt.darius_hieroglyphs.yoyotte1973','Les inscriptions hiéroglyphiques égyptiennes de la statue de Darius à Suse','SCHOLARLY_EDITION',2,'Académie des Inscriptions et Belles-Lettres / Persée','Jean Yoyotte','lang.en','1973','2026-08-26','https://www.persee.fr/doc/crai_0065-0536_1973_num_117_2_12879','CRAI 117-2, pp. 256-266','Article copyright and Persée terms apply; metadata, locators and independent summaries only','Preliminary scholarly publication of the Egyptian inscription program','Do not reproduce the article or figures in bulk',0,'French article; Egyptian hieroglyphic texts discussed','URL_SYNTAX_VALID','Primary scholarly anchor for the Egyptian-language program and its royal-theological interpretation.'),
('source.iranica.susa_achaemenid','Susa iii. The Achaemenid Period','SCHOLARLY_REFERENCE',2,'Encyclopaedia Iranica','Rémy Boucharlat','lang.en','2009-07-20','2026-08-26','https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/susa-iii-the-achaemenid-period/','SUSA iii','Encyclopaedia Iranica rights apply; metadata and independent summaries only','Scholarly synthesis of the archaeological and inscription context','No bulk reproduction',0,'English scholarly reference','URL_SYNTAX_VALID','Identifies DSab, the Egyptian origin, Heliopolis destination, Susa transfer, base symbolism and labelled subject peoples.'),
('source.iranica.epigraphy_old_persian','Epigraphy i. Old Persian and Middle Iranian epigraphy','SCHOLARLY_REFERENCE',2,'Encyclopaedia Iranica',NULL,'lang.en',NULL,'2026-08-26','https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/epigraphy-i/','EPIGRAPHY i','Encyclopaedia Iranica rights apply; metadata and independent summaries only','Scholarly epigraphic overview','No bulk reproduction',0,'English scholarly reference','URL_SYNTAX_VALID','States that DSab is trilingual and accompanied by five hieroglyphic texts, including a province list.'),
('source.persia.dsab.achemenet','Susa: Central Part of the Statue','SCHOLARLY_PROJECT',3,'Achemenet / Musée du Louvre research network','Pierre Briant project','lang.en',NULL,'2026-08-26','https://www.achemenet.com/en/visit/?/susa/the-statue-of-darius/6=','DSab object presentation','Project website rights apply; metadata and independent summaries only','Scholarly object presentation with inscription placement and Vallat translation attribution','No images or extended modern translation packaged',0,'English presentation; ancient cuneiform languages identified','URL_SYNTAX_VALID','Confirms several inscriptions, the three imperial cuneiform languages and the DSab opening on the pleated robe.');

